@startuml ProjectStatus-State
hide empty description

title PTrack v0.1.0 — Project Status Lifecycle\n(status derived from stage per ADR-009)

[*] --> NoStatusSet : project created\n(stage = null)

state "No status set" as NoStatusSet
state "Not Started" as NotStarted
state "In Progress" as InProgress
state "Completed" as Completed

NoStatusSet --> NotStarted : stage set to Planning
NoStatusSet --> InProgress : stage set to Analysis,\nDesign, Implementation,\nor Testing
NoStatusSet --> Completed  : stage set to Done

NotStarted --> InProgress  : stage changed to Analysis,\nDesign, Implementation,\nor Testing
NotStarted --> Completed   : stage changed to Done
NotStarted --> NoStatusSet : stage cleared\n[not applicable in v0.1.0\n— stage cannot be unset]

InProgress --> NotStarted  : stage changed to Planning
InProgress --> Completed   : stage changed to Done
InProgress --> InProgress  : stage changed to another\nmid-development stage

Completed --> NotStarted   : stage changed to Planning
Completed --> InProgress   : stage changed to Analysis,\nDesign, Implementation,\nor Testing

note "All transitions are triggered by\nthe user selecting a stage from\nthe stage dropdown (UC-STG-001).\nstatus is never set directly by the user\n(ADR-009). On save failure the stage\n(and therefore the status) reverts to\nits previous value (FR-STG-001 AC3)." as N1

@enduml
